<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Icel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th or 6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Icel is the ancestor from whom the kings of Mercia traced their descent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> genealogies, which make him a descendant of the continental Anglian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/offa-of-mercia">Offa</a> of Angel. He may have led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angles">Angles</a> across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> in the late 5th or early 6th century, but nothing is known of him beyond his name, and the Mercian royal house was sometimes called the Iclingas after him.</p></div>
